### 2026-08-29 - Split Milestone 2 and write the 2A design

**What changed:** Split Milestone 2 into 2A (content injection, capture, and the
companion panel) and 2B (Markdown serialization, versioned download, vault write,
and the offer to move to Processed). Wrote and approved
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-29-milestone-2a-design.md`. No code changed.
**Why:** The two halves fail differently. 2A fails when Substack renames a class,
so its evidence is fixtures and visible failure states. 2B fails when a
serializer has a bug, so its evidence is pure unit tests. One spec would have
mixed the two testing strategies and let a stall on Substack's DOM block work
that has nothing to do with Substack. Items 3 to 5 never needed the article page
anyway; they hang off the board's existing detail panel.

The design overturns three earlier decisions, each recorded in its "Amendments to
earlier documents" section. The panel is `chrome.sidePanel`, not the iframe the
Milestone 1 design committed to, because the side panel reaches the same
extension origin and the same Dexie without becoming a co-tenant in Substack's
layout. Native Save moves to Milestone 3, because its value is unrealizable until
the Saved-list parser exists, its popover cannot be fixture-tested, and Milestone
3 has to build the same inverted-label driver for Unsave regardless. Signed-out
becomes a note rather than a gate, because the spike found metadata reads without
a session and 2A invokes no native control.

Injection is `activeTab` plus `scripting`, with no host permissions and no
declarative content script. This is the only option that reaches custom-domain
publications, which a `*://*.substack.com/*` match is structurally blind to,
without asking for `<all_urls>`.
